.TH INTENSEFLOW 6 "November 2026" "Intenseflow" "Games"

.SH NAME
intenseflow \- source port of id Software's Wolfenstein 3D and Spear of Destiny

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B intenseflow
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Intenseflow
is an open-source port of id Software's classic first-person shooter
.B Wolfenstein 3D
and its prequel
.B Spear of Destiny
to the cross-platform multimedia library
.BR "Simple DirectMedia Layer (SDL)" .
It is meant to keep the original feel while taking advantage of some improvements.
Intenseflow is based on Wolf4SDL.

The game files are not part of Intenseflow. At startup, the engine looks for a complete set of
game files and picks the first game that is found, in this order:
.BR wl6 ,
.BR sod ,
.BR wl3 ,
.B wl1
and
.BR sdm .
The game is identified by the file name extension of its data files:
.TP
.B wl6
Wolfenstein 3D, full version (six episodes)
.TP
.B sod
Spear of Destiny, full version
.TP
.B wl3
Wolfenstein 3D, three episode Apogee release
.TP
.B wl1
Wolfenstein 3D, shareware version (one episode)
.TP
.B sdm
Spear of Destiny, demo version
.PP
The additional Spear of Destiny mission disks use the extensions
.BR sd1 ,
.B sd2
and
.BR sd3 ,
see the
.B \-\-mission
option.

If the name of the executable contains a dash followed by one of the above game names, for
example when it is started through a symbolic link called
.BR intenseflow\-sod ,
this game is chosen as if the
.B \-\-game
option had been given.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Prints a short help page and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints version information and exits.
.TP
\fB\-\-game\fR <name>
Uses the data files of the given game, one of
.BR wl6 ,
.BR sod ,
.BR wl3 ,
.B wl1
or
.BR sdm .
By default, the first game found is used, in that order.
.TP
\fB\-\-mission\fR <mission>
Plays the given mission of Spear of Destiny, from 0 to 3
(default: 0, which uses the files with the extension
.BR sod ,
while 1 to 3 use
.BR sd1 ,
.B sd2
or
.BR sd3 ).
.TP
\fB\-\-tedlevel\fR <level>
Starts the game in the given level.
.TP
.B \-\-baby
Sets the difficulty to baby for
.BR \-\-tedlevel .
.TP
.B \-\-easy
Sets the difficulty to easy for
.BR \-\-tedlevel .
.TP
.B \-\-normal
Sets the difficulty to normal for
.BR \-\-tedlevel .
.TP
.B \-\-hard
Sets the difficulty to hard for
.BR \-\-tedlevel .
.TP
.B \-\-nowait
Skips the intro screens.
.TP
.B \-\-demotest
Skips right into the demo loop.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Starts the game in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-nograbmouse
Does not grab the mouse in windowed mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-res\fR <width> <height>
Sets the screen resolution, which must be a multiple of 320x200.
.TP
\fB\-\-resf\fR <w> <h>
Sets any screen resolution of at least 320x200, which may result in graphic errors.
.TP
\fB\-\-joystick\fR <index>
Uses the index\-th joystick if available
(\-1 disables the joystick, default: 0).
.TP
\fB\-\-joystickhat\fR <index>
Enables movement with the given coolie hat.
.TP
\fB\-\-samplerate\fR <rate>
Sets the sound sample rate in Hz (default: 44100).
.TP
\fB\-\-audiobuffer\fR <size>
Sets the size of the audio buffer, which determines the sound latency,
in bytes (default: 2048 / (44100 / samplerate)).
.TP
.B \-\-ignorenumchunks
Ignores the number of chunks in the VGAHEAD file, which may be useful for some broken mods.
.TP
\fB\-\-configdir\fR <dir>
Sets the directory where the configuration file and the saved games are stored
(default: the user data directory of SDL, see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BR \-\-goobers ", " \-\-debugmode
Enables the debug keys, which are accessed with the Tab key.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./
The current directory is searched for game files first.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/games/wolf3d
Searched for game files after the current directory. If
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is not set, it defaults to
.IR $HOME/.local/share .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_DIRS/games/wolf3d
Searched for game files last, once for each directory of the list. If
.B XDG_DATA_DIRS
is not set, it defaults to
.IR /usr/local/share:/usr/share .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/intenseflow
The default directory for the configuration file
.I intenseflow.cfg
and the saved games, unless the
.B \-\-configdir
option is given. The configuration file is the same for all games, the names of the saved
games carry the extension of the game that is played. On Windows, the directory of the
executable is used instead if it is writable, and the user data directory of SDL otherwise.

